WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.272
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.360
So we've got our
basic Shiny navbarPage.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:21.240
And pretty much, any
navbarPage that you've seen,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:26.430
you'll probably notice that
you're constricted to the fact

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:32.910
that each one of these tab links
has to link to content inside 

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.570
of that page.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.870
So we haven't
really provided you

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.640
with a way to officially provide
another link here that maybe

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.960
links to some external website.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.150
Or what if you wanted to
have a right-aligned nav

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:56.460
item that links to a login
page or something like that?

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.910
Historically, there's been
no way to do this officially

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.140
with Shiny.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:06.840
So I've seen people come
up with pretty crazy hacks

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.240
to make this possible,
which was part

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.655
of the motivation for doing
this in the first place.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:19.310
But bslib provides this
new API, essentially,

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:26.240
that replaces tabPanel and
navbarPage and navbarMenu--

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.770
the basic building
blocks that you

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:30.950
may have used to create a
navbarPage or a tabsetPanel

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.040
or something like that.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.250
So with the new
interface, it's called--

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:39.260
instead of tabPanel,
you say nav.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.750
We give it a title,
give it some content.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.400
There's also a nav_item.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.250
It basically just takes whatever
you give it and places it

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.340
directly in that nav heading.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.520
So you could do something
like provide a hyperlink

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.870
to Shiny's GitHub
page or wherever

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:03.830
you want to provide a link to.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:10.240
There's actually also ways of
using this to include something

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.460
like text input box, which
would allow you to implement

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:17.890
something like a search
feature in your Shiny app

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:19.780
where somebody could type in.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.030
In the navbar at the top, they
could search for something.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.390
And then you could wire
that up to some server logic

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:32.050
to show something as people are
typing, something like that.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:35.720
There's also this
nav_spacer where

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.180
it's like the name suggests.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:43.490
It just adds spacing in between
one set of nav_nav_items

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:46.430
and another set
of nav_nav_items.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.860
So by putting the
nav-spacer here,

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:52.340
this will basically
left-align all of this--

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.320
all of these, like the a and the
b and the Shiny external link.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.210
And then it will write a line--

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:03.890
this nav_menu--
that has other links

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.560
to more content within
the page and then another

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.380
nav_item to link to some
other external content.

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:18.020
And this is a fancy way
of reducing duplication

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:22.880
for this particular example,
where this nav_item's function

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:27.900
will return a list of
these nav_items essentially

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:33.420
so that I can use
this rlang splicing

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:38.280
operator to essentially splice
in the list of nav_items

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.400
into this navbarPage.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.300
There's also another argument
to navbar that allows you to--

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.000
like, if you have
some content that you

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:53.330
want to show regardless of
what nav_item is selected

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.950
in a navbarPage, you can use--

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:00.140
there's a header and a footer
to say, always show this content

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.870
above or below the
other content that

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:07.980
is dependent on whatever
tab is selected.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:12.470
So I'm using that to also show
these other functions that

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.800
can consume a
collection of nav_items

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:19.160
called navs_tab, navs_pill.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.230
So these two
functions essentially

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:30.170
replace tabsetPanel for
creating that basic tab look

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.360
or also with pills.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.900
And there's also variants on
these called navs_tab_card

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:40.850
and navs_pill_card,
which I'll just show you

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.830
how these actually look.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.300
So here's the first
navs_tab here.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.820
So this is like the kind
of classic tabsetPanel

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:53.780
look that we're used
to seeing everywhere

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:58.110
with the ability to flip through
the tab a and tab b content.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.940
I also have this
Shiny link here,

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:03.290
which will take me to
Shiny's GitHub page

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.770
as well as the
right-aligned menu

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.500
with the other external
link and some other content.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.680
So I've taken the same nav_items
essentially and placed them

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:19.100
inside of this page_navbar
to get the top level a and b

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.430
content.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.730
So I can flip back
and forth here.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:24.350
And then this is
the footer content

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:27.740
with those other
variants for rendering

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.530
a collection of nav_items.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:34.970
So here's the navs_tab,
the navs_pill.

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.670
I do like this a little
bit generally better

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:42.320
than the basic tabsetPanel
look in general.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:49.980
But I think part of the reason
why tabsetPanel doesn't always

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:53.130
look great is the
fact that there

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:58.740
is no padding between this
content here and the border.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.050
And there's also-- the
border doesn't extend

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.510
around the content either.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:08.280
So it looks like there's
content floating in space.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:13.120
And it's also smashed together.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.380
So that's why we've
provided this navs_tab_card

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.250
and navs_pill_card to add
some border around all

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:25.740
of the content and add some
padding between that top order

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.200
and the actual content inside.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.920
So for all functional
purposes, these

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:38.010
provide the same
functional experience.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:41.610
But this is just designed in a
slightly different way where it

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.040
has a real container around it.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:49.530
It has a real header
to it in the sense

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:52.920
that it's got this
gray background holding

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.015
the tabs and the pills.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.970
And you may have seen something
like this already with--

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:04.660
I believe in Shiny this
is called navlistPanel.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:08.760
But I'm now calling
it navs_pill_list.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.110
And there might be--
like, in the future,

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:15.540
there might be other different
variants that render things

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.080
in slightly different ways.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.750
But this is more of
a sidebar approach

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:27.780
where you can get those
nav_items stacked vertically

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:30.510
and then the content
on the right.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:33.720
And actually, these
functions are now

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.760
used by Shiny
underneath the hood when

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.370
you use tabPanel or navbarPage.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.940
So now, the actual logic
for all of that stuff

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.580
lives inside of bslib.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:51.330
But we've also built out the API
to allow you to do more with it

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:55.920
and design this functional
interface to allow

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:01.185
us to continue building more
ways to render navigation

00:08:01.185 --> 00:08:04.500
items essentially.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.550
[MUSIC PLAYING]

